/passage/?search=Esther+1&version=NIV (document: fetch_page-f8b7c37c5fced428)\n23. Esther 1 NIV - Queen Vashti Deposed - This is what - Bible Gateway — https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Esther+1&version=NIV (document: fetch_page-3370e793746339d5)\n\n## Claim Register\n\n- (accepted, critical=true) The Book of Esther (NIV) first mentions a place by name; the location of the events is present-day Iran. [6]\n- (accepted, critical=true) Ahasuerus was a great king of Persia. [7]\n- (accepted, critical=false) The events of the Book of Esther fit chronologically between the 6th and 7th chapters of Ezra. [6]\n- (accepted, critical=false) Ahasuerus had an extensive empire with 127 provinces from India to Ethiopia. [6]\n- (accepted, critical=false) Mohammad Reza Shah Pahlavi was the last king of Iran and ruled Iran until 1979. [8]\n- (accepted, critical=true) Amīr ʿAbbas Hoveyda was the prime minister of Iran under Shah Mohammed Reza Pahlavi from January 1965 to August 1977. [9]\n- (accepted, critical=true) Hoveyda's tenure as prime minister ended in August 1977, meaning he was no longer prime minister in April 1977. [9]\n- (accepted, critical=false) The Book of Esther (NIV) mentions India and Cush as the extent of Xerxes' 127 provinces. [13]\n- (accepted, critical=false) The Book of Esther (NIV) mentions Susa as the citadel where King Xerxes reigned. [14]\n",
